<title>UK: Hicking Pentecost H1 pretax rises 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Hicking Pentecost H1 pretax rises 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		12.4		   vs 11.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.4		    vs 2.1</p>
<p> Pretax		     3.84		   vs 3.40</p>
<p> Turnover		   49.7		   vs 39.34</p>
<p>NOTE - UK textiles, industrial threads and products group Hicking Pentecost Plc, which brought its results forward because of a number of profit disappointments in the sector, said it expected an &quot;equally robust&quot; H2 performance. October sales had been good and order books were promising.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 4.56		   vs 3.64</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.73		   vs 0.24</p>
<p> Tax charge		 0.90		   vs 0.80</p>
<p> Attributable	     2.93		   vs 2.60</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 7, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  Dec 17</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Dec 9</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
